<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 100,000 -USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 100,000 -USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts Thursday were 100,000 head, compared with 99,000 a week ago and 89,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were mostly $1.50 per cwt lower than mid-session Wednesday. Trade was moderate and demand light to moderate with light to moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    56.50 -57.50	   57.50 -58.50</p>
<p>few			56.00  58.00		    59.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    55.50 -57.50	   56.00 -58.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
